# Better Auth (ADR-017, ADR-021)

- Only `packages/auth` imports `better-auth` / `@better-auth/*`. Frontends use
  `@eleva/auth/client`, `@eleva/auth/server` (`getSession()`) and `@eleva/auth/proxy`
  (`getSessionCookie()`). Never instantiate `betterAuth()` in an app.
- Mount path is `/auth` on `apps/api` (`basePath: "/auth"`). Product-app cookie domain is
  `.eleva.care`. From Phase 12, `admin.eleva.care` uses a host-only `__Host-` cookie and
  rejects the shared cookie (ADR-015 / ADR-017). `trustedOrigins` is an explicit list —
  never `*`.
- Every new permission goes in `packages/auth/src/permissions.ts` (`createAccessControl`)
  and a role grant. `capabilities.ts` derives from that file. Product label =
  `(organization.type, member.role)`.
- Regenerate schema with the Better Auth CLI into `packages/db/src/schema/auth`. Hand edits
  are indexes, RLS class headers and `additionalFields` only.
- Wrap `databaseHooks` side effects in `withAudit()`. Personal Space name is
  `{firstName}'s Space`.
- `requireApiAuth` accepts exactly one credential: session cookie (origin-checked),
  `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`, or `x-api-key`. Cross-mode is 400.
- Calendar tokens: `auth.api.getAccessToken({ body: { accountId, userId } })` —
  persist both on the connection; do not store tokens in `packages/calendar`.
- WorkOS helpers, Widgets and `infra/workos` are Phase 3 deletions (removed, see ADR-017).
  Do not add new WorkOS calls.

Load the **better-auth** skill to add a plugin, permission or trusted origin.
